  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nUpper air pattern showing an upper ridge over most of the country\nwith a very strong upper low over the Gulf of Alaska. Said upper\nridge will help to heat things through Saturday across northeast\nMontana as nearly full sun and rising 500 mb heights will allow \ntemps to be warmer or much warmer than what they were Thursday \nwith highs today in the 90s most places. Look for highs Saturday \nto be 90s in the northeast with 100-110 elsewhere. A Excessive \nHeat Watch remains in effect for Saturday and Saturday night.\n\nThe strong upper low over the Gulf of Alaska will move east\ntranslating to an upper trough over west-central Canada by\nTuesday. This will send a couple of cool fronts across the area,\nthe first one arriving early Sunday morning with the second\npushing through Monday morning. Wind will signal their arrival as\nonly small chances of brief showers are expected Sunday night.\nThe wind with the leftover warm air late Saturday and Sunday \ncould result in Fire Weather issues. A Fire Weather Watch remains\nin effect for this period. Windy conditions Saturday night through\nMonday will also likely need a Lake Wind Advisory.\n\nAfter Monday, the upper trough moves east and a zonal flow\nsuccumbs a bit to a Desert southwest ridge by the end of the\nforecast cycle. Expect dry conditions with temperatures warming to\nnear normal. Winds generally look light so Fire Weather issues\nshould be minimal.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nHigh confidence in the hot weather Friday and Saturday. \nConfidence is moderate to high for critical fire weather \nconditions Sunday. Low confidence in amounts and timing of  \nshowers Sunday night.\n\nNo major changes were made from the base forecast with this\nforecast package. TFJ",
